        "author": {
          "handle": "owen",
          "id": "user-owen",
          "name": "Owen Zeng"
        },
        "body": "The real source note is in Slack around the Plaid/OAuth rollout. QA is worried our release checklist missed paths from that note; please reconstruct the checklist from Slack and prove the implementation covers it.",
        "created_at": "2026-06-07T14:00:00Z",
        "id": "comment-1"
      },
      {
        "author": {
          "handle": "maya",
          "id": "user-maya",
          "name": "Maya Chen"
        },
        "body": "Please include the evidence generated by the repo's local validation in the handoff; QA needs enough detail to trace what changed and what was verified.",
        "created_at": "2026-06-07T14:02:00Z",
        "id": "comment-2"
      },
      {
        "author": {
          "handle": "maya",
          "id": "user-maya",
          "name": "Maya Chen"
        },
        "body": "GitHub repo acme/oauth-qa-matrix has the application snapshot. Use the repo docs/tests to find the affected implementation, open and merge a local GitHub PR after CI passes, and link the merged PR here.",
        "created_at": "2026-06-07T12:07:00Z",
        "id": "comment-github-1"
      },
      {
        "author": {
          "handle": "maya",
          "id": "user-maya",
          "name": "Maya Chen"
        },
        "body": "Use the normal on-call workflow: start the active issue before coding if it is still Todo, open a local GitHub PR, wait for its CI to pass, merge it, include the actual merged PR URL in the Slack and ticket handoff, and then move the issue to In Review. Per team convention, name the incident branch and the PR title or body after the issue id (for example ops-503-...) so support can trace the change from the GitHub side.",
        "created_at": "2026-06-07T12:08:00Z",
        "id": "comment-workflow-v5"
      }
    ],
